 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "The PDF has a broken cross-reference table (pdfplumber cannot open it; pypdf and pdfium can); it was re-saved with pypdf for parsing and every page image was rendered from the original file. Tables (PDF pages 6 to 11): cell text parsed from the text layer with pdfplumber, the location of each row from its background colour sampled on the rendered page (legend: OPD pink, IPD blue, ICU yellow, SRCLI purple). Recorded rows (pages 10 and 11) were compared value by value with the rendered pages by overlaying the parsed text on the page image (scale 3): no differences. Organism charts (pages 6 to 10) are vector graphics: each bar was matched to its legend entry by identical fill colour (bar order equals legend order in every box; five bars drawn with pattern fills were matched by that order) and to its data label by position; every box was compared with the page image. Every recorded row n agrees with the chart counts (for example urine OPD E. coli 976, E. faecalis 218, E. faecium 208; Klebsiella spps 94 = K. pneumoniae 85 + K. oxytoca 9). Page numbers are PDF page numbers."
 },
 "notes": "Dr. RMLIMS Lucknow Microbiology News Letter, Issue 6 (March 2019), antibiograms for January to December 2018 by specimen, each organism row belonging to one location (OPD, IPD recorded as wards, ICU, or SRCLI) shown only by the row colour. SRCLI (State Referral Centre for Laboratory Investigation, as the report defines it) is a separate location category and is not recorded. To reach 30 isolates the report groups organisms: \"Lactose fermenters\" (E. coli, Citrobacter, Klebsiella, Proteus and Providencia spp.), \"Non lactose fermenters\" (Pseudomonas and Acinetobacter spp.) and \"Staphylococcus spps\" (S. aureus and CoNS); these rows have no organism key and are not recorded, so this edition contributes only urine rows (E. coli, Klebsiella, Citrobacter and Enterobacter spp., E. faecium and E. faecalis). Specimens as printed: blood; \"Body fluids\" = sterile body fluids including CSF (recorded as sterile body fluids); \"Respiratory specimen\" = sputum, BAL, throat swab, nasal swab, bronchial aspirate, endotracheal aspirate; \"Pus and other samples\" = pus, pus swab, catheter tip, CVP line, shunt, tissue, bone marrow, vaginal fluid, semen, ear discharge, ear swab, endometrial discharge, vaginal swab, stool, urethral swab (recorded as pus); urine. The report notes that samples without clinical details were excluded from the antibiogram analysis (samples analysed are fewer than received). Organism counts are the OPD, IPD and ICU chart labels; the build adds \"Pseudomonas species\" to P. aeruginosa, \"Acinetobacter species\" to A. baumannii and \"Citrobacter diversus\" to C. koseri, as its organism keys do. The live URL returns 404; the PDF was downloaded from the Internet Archive copy of the same URL.",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: all 162 cells (the seeded sample of 40 included), all 10 row n values and all 10 row locations re-read against the page images (PDF pages 10 and 11, rendered at scale 4); 0 errors, nothing corrected.",
  "Row locations from the row fill colours in the PDF vector content against the page legend (OPD pink, IPD blue, ICU yellow, SRCLI purple): all 10 agree.",
  "Counts: all 242 re-derived independently from the vector bar charts (PDF pages 6 to 10, from a copy of the original re-saved with pdfium): each bar matched to its legend entry by identical fill colour (pattern-filled bars to the single pattern legend square of their box; bar order equals legend order in every box), its value taken from the data label and cross-checked against bar height over the chart unit. 242 of 242 agree in organism and value.",
  "115 of the counts (blood ICU; respiratory IPD and ICU; pus OPD and IPD; urine OPD) were also read by eye on the charts rendered at scale 6: no differences.",
  "Intrinsic cells confirmed as printed: urine OPD Enterobacter spp. (n 43) AS 23, CZ 19, CX 33.",
  "Chart bars left out as the excluded list says were confirmed at the listed values: urine OPD K. pneumoniae 85 (the OPD table row is Klebsiella spps 94 = 85 + K. oxytoca 9) and every Acinetobacter lwoffii and Chryseobacterium indologenes bar. The build reports no count-table mismatch."
 ],
